Exercise: Count employees in each department having more than 5 employees. 

Solution: We used LEFT JOIN to connect the Department and EmployeeDepartmentHistory tables, to list all departments and count the number of employees.
The COUNT was GROUPed BY the department Name, and the HAVING clause filtered out the departments having less than 5 employees.


Tables used
[AdventureWorks2022].[HumanResources].[Department]
[AdventureWorks2022].[HumanResources].[EmployeeDepartmentHistory]

Functions used
COUNT

T-SQL code
USE AdventureWorks2022;
GO

SELECT Departments.[Name]
	  ,COUNT(EmployeesHistorical.[BusinessEntityID]) AS NumberEmployees
FROM [AdventureWorks2022].[HumanResources].[Department] AS Departments
LEFT JOIN [AdventureWorks2022].[HumanResources].[EmployeeDepartmentHistory] AS EmployeesHistorical
ON Departments.[DepartmentID] = EmployeesHistorical.[DepartmentID]
GROUP BY Departments.[Name]
HAVING COUNT(EmployeesHistorical.[BusinessEntityID]) > 5


